WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
GoNuts hive setup: two accounts, one shared panel.
Use two launcher instances on the same PC. Headless is optional.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:22.000
1. Start in the instance whose trading history you want to keep.
Disconnect, then open Multiplayer > GoNuts hive.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:34.000
2. Click Create hive & copy code. Your data stays in its original folder.
Close and reopen this first instance once.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:46.000
3. Open GoNuts hive in a fresh second instance.
Click Paste code, then Join hive. Use a different Minecraft account.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:58.000
4. Hive linked: close and reopen the second instance.
Existing local history is never silently merged or overwritten.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:10.000
5. Enable the web panel in Autopilot > WEB on the first instance.
Start both accounts; the shared panel can view and control either account.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Keep the original shared folder. Logins and proxies stay local.
Full instructions and troubleshooting: cody-raves.github.io/Gonuts/guide/#hive
